Hello All,
   I've been using NHSOUND for a week or so now and its NEATO.  For
those unfamiliar with this its a little TSR one runs before starting NH
on IBM PCs with SoundBlaster cards.  
   Problems I initially had running were solved by putting the
ct-voice.drv that come with YOUR soundblaster as opposed to the one
provided with it, since I believe it differs from the original
soundblaster, SBPro, and the SB 16 series (which I'm using it with).
Also a warning should be given with the NHSOUND.CNF file.  This is the
file where you set up what topline text will trigger what sounds and
depending on ones amount of expanded memory, you can have upto 100 such
triggering events and sounds!  Make sure none of the VOC files are
bigger than 32,000 k or the install will fail.  Also make sure you
follow the exact format he states for including the sounds.
   I've now got 76 sounds going (probably more like 50 something but
each triggering phrase counts as a seperate entry i.e. make fountain
sounds for each of the fountain on level warnings).  Although game play
isn't stopped while the sound plays, it does appear on my 4meg machine
that game play is significantly slowed while when back at a mere 30 or
so sounds there was no appearant slowdown.
   Having not gotten a reply from the author of this program yet I'm
still looking for other users out there with a cool ensemble of VOC
files (I'll show you mine if you show me yours!).  Also does anyone know
a cool ftp site for WAV or VOC sound effect files.  
   Oh by the way, you can get this deal at f.ms.uky.edu in the msdos
music section (yea I guess it's  a sound related deal but still).

